Z||000007||BBBAD GT||07-28-2000||07:10 PM||||I'll hopefully get some ET's soon, the only thing holding me back is the Isuzu 5 speed in it already.  Chris says its doing fine back there, but he hasn't 'abused' it yet.  Archie says it should hold per his website, but I'm a little leary.  It needs some sort of wing (maybe factory or an IMSA type), but that'll be later (any opinions?).  <P>I'll be selling the 87 GT as soon as I'm comfortable with driving the V8 daily.  <P>I keep telling myself "Do I need another rip roaring V8 in the garage?".....of course I do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||6
Z||000008||LAMBO||07-28-2000||07:24 PM||||Normally, I'd go for the wing look in a second, but, in this case, your new ride looks awsome the way it is. I might become a notchback fan yet.<BR>Lambo||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||07-29-2000||01:51 AM||||Great looking car. I'd definately put a wing on it but I really like notchbacks with wings.||||reg||14
Z||000010||BAM-BAM||07-29-2000||02:35 AM|||| I would go with the " YOU ARE WHAT YOU EAT" theory, and you'll be eating a few mustangs, so do my 2000 Mustang spoiler mod and have it glassed in. I seriously would glass it into the deck. It really adds an awesome line to the notchback; not really sure that it would look right on a fastback though. Excellent buy and good luck from here on out. You got an awesome ride.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 07-29-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000011||kevin||07-29-2000||08:14 PM||||EXELLENT! I'm jealous,very envious. My opinion is to stay away from the wing. The reason you are hearing the positive  comments about your ride is because of the way it sits; the attractive wheel/tire combo, the bright red paint and the slight custom side air intake. Keep it the way it is, and you will continue to stand out in the crowd of ordinary cars. Smooth is best. Like a baby but and ...(.)(.) You know what I mean?   ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Homicidal||07-29-2000||08:18 PM||||I agree 100%!  I am so tired of seeing a lowered car with rims and giant spoiler.  I usually say that Fieros like that look BETTER with spoliers.  But not in this case.  The absence of a spolier gives it that stroke of originality!||||reg||1
