Z||000021||BBBAD GT||07-30-2000||04:07 PM||||I've asked Chris to post about your questions about the side custom scoops.  I forgot what he told me it was, but I love it too.  <P>'NO WING' is winning so far.......<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Sillhouette.com||07-30-2000||04:29 PM||||I would keep the 87GT with the better pop up lights bigger fueltank and better windshield washer tank and just swap the V8 into it using the Monzie that is already in there (if it has a manusl).  That would solve your Isuzu problem you would be building your own pride and there is nothing more eyepleasing than a well built fastback.    <P>Oh yeah no wing be it fast back or notch back.<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000023||Chris McDonald||07-31-2000||02:24 AM||||The side scoops will be a little difficult to duplicate.  I pulled them off the front fenders of a second generation Z-28, flipped them around backwards and frenched them into the Fiero panels.  Per G.M. and the Camaro resto companies there are no N.O.S. or aftermarket scoops being produced.  <P>If you like the look start combing your local salvage yard.  I happened to luck up a good deal on these two scoops, but the going price is about $150 each. You will have to fight the Camaro guys to get some. <P>I always thought the car could use a wing just to stay with the G.T. looks.  However, wings tend to date cars to the 1980s.  Contemporary design tends to flow with body enhanced spoilers and lower profile looks.<P>I guess it is just personal preference.  <P>Thanks for the nice compliments.  I will really miss this car.  I think Jeff is going to give it a great home and maybe some way cool future modifications as he sees fit.  <P>Chris    <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Philphine||07-31-2000||03:42 AM||||had to go back and look at the picture again. those are the scoops i used on the front for radiator cooling assist.i thought about using them in back but thought it would be too hard to do. i think i'll look for another set and try it.<P>plus i vote for a mustang wing too. mustangs are close enough in rear demensions that the wings fit and look good on fieros, plus there are more style selections. you could go more conservative than the one you showed fron ebay. i have a coupe/conv. saleen wing on my '87 (the old style) and plan to get an f40 wing for my '84.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||Archie||07-31-2000||07:31 AM||||I think the car looks perfect.<P>Those TSW Blades are my all time favorite wheel.<P>My vote is for no Wing.<P>Archie||||reg||14
Z||000026||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||08:33 AM||||Jeff, let me know when your here i'll get you straped down on the dyno before you go... where "just north of ATL" will you be? I vote no wing... ||||reg||1
Z||000027||BBBAD GT||07-31-2000||12:46 PM||||Jeez Travis......you're strapping the car down before I even pick it up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Actually, I just want to get it home before I do anything to it, but thanks for the offer tho.  I'll email you with specific directions to where I'll be at (I'm still not sure where yet).  <P>For the record, no wing is growing on me.  I hope to have it up to the ElPaso IL show on 8/26.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||6
