Z||000034||Cliff Pennock||07-31-2000||07:32 PM||||I thought I'd help you with the wing question:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/withwing.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wowing.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||12
Z||000035||Formula||07-31-2000||08:14 PM||||wow, cliff flew all the way from holland to put a wing on your car to see how it looked.. Im starting to think cliff may be superman?????????  I would have to say I like it with the wing better, you should get some formula wheels on it and give a guy named formula that hangs out here those tsw blades :0)  LOL..... nobody ever falls for that one, anyways sweet ride dood..<P>drool.........||||reg||1
Z||000036||batboy||07-31-2000||08:26 PM||||The Isuzu tranny will be just fine if you don't abuse it. Any Fiero tranny will have a shortened lifespan if abused with that much torque. You have to learn to go easy on the launches. If you're spinning and squealing the tires, you ain't getting traction anyway. If you do run it at the dragstrip, drive around the water box. I repeat, do not do any burnouts. Resist the temptation to show off. I have an auto, but I still take it easy at the start. I launch with no wheel spin, careful to stay out of the 4 barrels until I'm hooked up good and moving, then I nail it.||||reg||1
Z||000037||Archie||07-31-2000||10:54 PM||||I agree with you on the launch at the drag strip. But, I've never been able to drive around the water box.<P>Archie<P>BTW, I still say no wing. Without the luggage racks the coupes look great w/o wings.||||reg||1
Z||000038||BBBAD GT||07-31-2000||11:22 PM||||Cliff:  Thanks for taking the time and doing the wing/no wing thing...however you did that.  I think I'm going to keep it without wing for now (majority rules too).<P>Batboy:  Thanks for the advice.  I don't normally go in the burnbox with street tires, the water gets in the grooves of the tires and drips at the starting line.  I've headed straight for the tree on launch (with the Stang of course) at times with a street tire guy dripping water ahead of me in line (not fun).  <P>BTW, what do you run the 1/4mi in Batboy?  Just curious...I'm predicting a basically stock 350 in a light Fiero would turn an easy 13.8 @ 102 with decent driving.  Anybody have V8 Fiero timeslips?  Archie?<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||6
Z||000039||Dan86gt3.8||07-31-2000||11:55 PM||||Does anybody know the going price for a pair of thoose tsw blades new????  And I too would love to see time slips!!!!!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
